config: add CONFIG_OPKG_NO_DISTFEEDS

The SBE1V1K image ships a fixed package set and has no matching upstream
package repository (custom kernel ABI).  Give the build an explicit switch
to write a placeholder /etc/opkg/distfeeds.conf instead of pointing at
downloads.openwrt.org feeds that cannot serve this ABI.

Apply from the buildroot top:  patch -p1 < 0011-...

--- a/config/Config-build.in
+++ b/config/Config-build.in
@@ -112,6 +112,16 @@
 		  This removes all ipkg/opkg status data files from the target directory
 		  before building the root filesystem.
 
+	config OPKG_NO_DISTFEEDS
+		bool
+		prompt "Do not generate distribution package feeds"
+		depends on !USE_APK
+		help
+		  Do not write /etc/opkg/distfeeds.conf.  Use this for images that
+		  ship a fixed package set and have no matching upstream package
+		  repository (for example a custom vendor target whose kernel ABI
+		  is not published on downloads.openwrt.org).
+
 	config IPK_FILES_CHECKSUMS
 		bool
 		prompt "Record files checksums in package metadata"
